<% if @account_blocked %>
  <%= header_section("Please add a different bank account for payouts.") %>
  <div>
    <p>Hi there. You recently added a bank account for Gumroad payouts, and our payment partner won't accept that particular account. There's nothing wrong with the details you entered — re-entering them won't help, and neither will waiting. We need you to add a <strong>different</strong> bank account.</p>
    <p>Please add another account you hold in <%= link_to "your payout settings", settings_payments_url %> — a different account at the same bank is fine. Once it's added we'll verify it, which clears this particular hold. Your payout settings will tell you if anything else still needs sorting out before we can pay you.</p>
    <p>If the account you tried is the only one you have, reply to this email and we'll look into it with you.</p>
  </div>
<% elsif @format_rejected %>
  <%= header_section("Your bank details need correcting for payouts.") %>
  <div>
    <p>Hi there. You recently added a bank account for Gumroad payouts, and our payment partner couldn't accept the details you entered — they don't match the format banks in your country use. Until they're corrected, we can't send you payouts.</p>
    <% if @expected_format_hint.present? %>
      <p>Here's the format your bank expects: <%= @expected_format_hint %></p>
      <p>Please re-enter your bank details in <%= link_to "your payout settings", settings_payments_url %>, matching that format exactly and without extra spaces. Waiting won't clear this one: we'll keep getting the same answer until the details themselves are updated, so it needs your edit.</p>
    <% else %>
      <p>Please check your account and bank code against what your bank shows and re-enter them in <%= link_to "your payout settings", settings_payments_url %>, without extra spaces. Waiting won't clear this one: we'll keep getting the same answer until the details themselves are updated, so it needs your edit.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% elsif @terminal_rejected %>
  <%= header_section("We need a different bank account for your payouts.") %>
  <div>
    <p>Hi there. You recently added a bank account for Gumroad payouts, and our payment partner won't accept that particular account. This isn't a typo: they've told us the account can't be used, either because payments or payouts to it have failed before or because they can't send payouts to that bank at all.</p>
    <p>Re-entering the same account won't change the answer, and this one won't clear on its own. To get your payouts moving, please add a different bank account in <%= link_to "your payout settings", settings_payments_url %> — another account at the same bank is fine, as is an account at a different bank.</p>
    <p>If a different account isn't an option for you, just reply to this email and we'll work out another way to pay you.</p>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <%= header_section("We couldn't verify your bank account yet.") %>
  <div>
    <p>Hi there. You recently added a bank account for Gumroad payouts, and we weren't able to verify it yet. This can happen if the account or routing details have a typo — or simply because a newly opened account, or a recently added bank or branch, isn't in our payment partner's records yet.</p>
    <p>First, double-check your details in <%= link_to "your payout settings", settings_payments_url %>. If you're confident everything is correct, you don't need to do anything: new accounts and banks usually appear within a few days to a few weeks, and we'll automatically re-check yours once a week for up to <%= RetryStripeRejectedPayoutSetupsJob::RETRY_WINDOW_WEEKS %> weeks. We'll only email you again if we still can't verify it.</p>
  </div>
<% end %>
